Capability gap found by the process-library case study for [process-library#337](https://github.com/ChemE-as-Code/process-library/issues/337) (scope tracker process-library#333).

## Gap

cheme has no particle-formation model. Mapping droplet drying and stickiness onto spray-dryer operating conditions (maltodextrin, droplet study doi:10.1016/j.foodres.2022.111049) needs:

- a single-droplet drying model: a characteristic drying curve or receding interface, shell (locking) formation, and surface temperature and moisture against time;
- a spray-dryer unit: the gas energy and humidity balance between inlet and outlet, and a bounded residence time from the dryer geometry and gas flow;
- a stickiness criterion on the droplet surface state, such as T_surface − T_g with Gordon–Taylor parameters, reported against the residence time;
- the inputs needed to reason about wall deposition: which dryer-scale measurements would be required, rather than a claimed deposition rate.

The case implements both models locally in `run.py` (process-library `benchmarks/reproductions/spray-drying-stickiness/`). Its reproduction fails under the frozen rule: 8 of 12 checks pass, and the cause of the t_glass bias is documented there. A core unit should start from a model that passes.

