## Problem

With #132714 and #141186, model lists come from Django and the Django builders fail without Go config. The sandbox agent still falls back to the legacy Python gateway when a run has no Go token, the `LLM_GATEWAY_*` settings remain, and several callers keep legacy-only branches.

## Changes

Removes the last runtime paths to the legacy gateway, so a missing Go configuration fails with a named error.

**Before**

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Run[sandbox run] --> Check{{"Go token and routed product?"}}
    Check -->|yes| Go[Go AI gateway]
    Check -->|no| Legacy[legacy Python gateway]
    classDef phBlue fill:#1d4aff,stroke:#1d4aff,color:#fff;
    classDef phRed fill:#f54e00,stroke:#f54e00,color:#fff;
    classDef phYellow fill:#f9bd2b,stroke:#f9bd2b,color:#000;
    classDef phGray fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#c7ccd1,color:#000;
    class Run phYellow;
    class Check phBlue;
    class Go,Legacy phRed;
```

**After**

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Run[sandbox run] --> Check{{"Go token and routed product?"}}
    Check -->|yes| Go[Go AI gateway]
    Check -->|no| Err[AiGatewayNotConfiguredError]
    classDef phBlue fill:#1d4aff,stroke:#1d4aff,color:#fff;
    classDef phRed fill:#f54e00,stroke:#f54e00,color:#fff;
    classDef phYellow fill:#f9bd2b,stroke:#f9bd2b,color:#000;
    classDef phGray fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#c7ccd1,color:#000;
    class Run,Err phYellow;
    class Check phBlue;
    class Go phRed;
```

- **Sandbox agent:** a gateway-billed run with no `AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN` or an unrouted product throws `AiGatewayNotConfiguredError` naming the missing setting. Own-subscription runs are unaffected.
- **Settings:** `LLM_GATEWAY_URL`, `LLM_GATEWAY_API_KEY` and `SANDBOX_LLM_GATEWAY_URL` are removed, and sandboxes no longer allow or probe the legacy hosts.
- Drops legacy `x-posthog-property-*` header branches in signals, conversations, stamphog, subscriptions, review_hog and the eval harness.
- **Desktop:** the proxy's legacy mode is gone, and `gateway_mode` leaves the "Task run started" event.
- **Telemetry:** the agent's `gateway_configured` attribute now means `AI_GATEWAY_URL` and `AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN` are both set, so subscription and unrouted runs report false.

## How did you test this code?

Agent, agent-contracts and harness suites, the desktop typecheck and the workspace-server agent and proxy suites pass. The gateway client, catalogue, agentsh, signals spend, Slack and organization suites pass apart from one test that needs local Redis. Not checked live.

## Release status

- No feature flag controls this change <!-- release-status: no-feature-flag -->

## Docs update

Agent skills and local-dev docs updated alongside the code.

## 🤖 Agent context

**Autonomy:** Human-driven (agent-assisted)

**Agent:** Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5. Requires human review.

